  "summary_en": "Japan's MLIT June 2024 guideline clarifying safety levels for Level 4 autonomous vehicles in limited-area unmanned mobility services. It sets a safety policy, vehicle typology by space and route, ODD definition, safe design requirements, risk scenarios and testing methods aligned with international (WP29, ISO) standards.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Applies to Level 4 vehicles applying for ODD grant; safety must prevent reasonably foreseeable preventable injury accidents",
   "Three vehicle types by space (limited/mixed) and route (fixed/wide) determine risk-scenario rigor",
   "Triple-unity safety: vehicle, infrastructure and surrounding road users",
   "Safe design: hazard perception, collision avoidance, 0.3G max deceleration with passengers, redundancy, obstacle detection",
   "Verification via risk scenarios, simulation and track/road tests, referencing ISO 26262, SOTIF, ISO 35402, WP29 SMS"
  ],
